# Verify before done

Do not end a turn or tell the user work is complete while verification is failing.

## Project verify config

Commands live in `.cursor/verify.json`:

```json
{
  "commands": [
    { "name": "test", "run": "go test ./...", "timeout": 120 },
    { "name": "lint", "run": "npm run lint", "optional": true }
  ]
}
```

- `name` — label in hook output
- `run` — shell command (repo root)
- `timeout` — seconds (default 300)
- `optional` — failure does not block (default false)

Empty `commands` is valid for a fresh template; add entries when the app has a test/lint script.

## Agent duties

After substantive code changes:

1. Run each non-optional command (or rely on the stop hook to force a retry loop).
2. Fix root cause; micro-commit fixes.
3. Re-run until green.

## Stop hook

`.cursor/hooks/verify-stop.sh` runs on every agent turn end. Failures auto-submit a follow-up (see rule-reinforcement). A clean tree with passing verify commands returns `{}` and stops the loop.
